      "message": "`runtime_probe` has already assume `mask` and `value` to contain exactly 1 byte of int.  Therefore, this kind of field schema change would break existing `runtiem_probe` in factory branches.\n\nHow about make the change backward compatible by adding new fields for multi-byte read:\n\n```\n                \"reg\": \"0x00\",\n                \"mask\": \"0x00\",\n                \"value\": \"0x00\",\n                \"multi_byte_mask\": \"0x0000ff00\",\n                \"multi_byte_value\": \"0x00004300\",\n```\n\nFor runtime probe built from old images, its behavior will not change.  For runtime probe built from ToT that read `multi_byte_*` fields, it can identify components better.",
